From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:00:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] block: asp: Find the storage endpoint on RTKit 10.2

The storage endpoint is the first app endpoint, which RTKit 11 and later
put at 0x20 and RTKit 10.2 at 6. The iPod touch 6 (A8, N102) runs the ANS
firmware of iOS 12.4, RTKit 10.2: take the endpoint from the protocol
version instead of always 0x20. RTKit 10.0 (endpoint 5) stays unsupported
and now says so.

The endpoint numbers are those of Nick Chan's ans1 driver
(HoolockLinux/linux ans1 ed8528f, 3b237c39df79).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
  drivers/block/asp.c |   18 +++++++++++++++---
  1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/block/asp.c b/drivers/block/asp.c
index ae1cc80..d4f7a0a 100644
--- a/drivers/block/asp.c
+++ b/drivers/block/asp.c
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 
 #define DEVICE_NAME	"asp"
 #define ASP_RTKIT_ENDPOINT	0x20
+#define ASP_RTKIT_ENDPOINT_V10_2	0x6
 #define DISK_NAME	"asp%dn%d"
 
 #define AKF_V1_REMAP_AP_LO	0x8
@@ -1174,14 +1175,25 @@ static void apple_asp_rtkit_recv(void *cookie, u8 endpoint, u64 message)
 static void apple_asp_rtkit_epmap_done(void *cookie)
 {
 	struct apple_asp *asp = cookie;
+	u16 major_ver, minor_ver;
 	int ret;
 
 	/*
 	 * The storage endpoint is the first app endpoint: 0x20 on RTKit 11 and
-	 * later (the iPad Air 2's ANS speaks 12.0). Older ANS firmware with
-	 * RTKit 10 is not supported; starting the endpoint fails there.
+	 * later (the iPad Air 2's ANS speaks 12.0), 6 on RTKit 10.2 (iOS 12's
+	 * ANS firmware on the iPod touch 6). RTKit 10.0 numbers it 5, which
+	 * RTKit here does not start app endpoints at: not supported.
 	 */
-	asp->ep = ASP_RTKIT_ENDPOINT;
+	apple_rtkit_protocol_version(asp->rtk, &major_ver, &minor_ver);
+	if (major_ver > 10)
+		asp->ep = ASP_RTKIT_ENDPOINT;
+	else if (major_ver == 10 && minor_ver >= 2)
+		asp->ep = ASP_RTKIT_ENDPOINT_V10_2;
+	else {
+		dev_err(asp->dev, "RTKit %u.%u is not supported", major_ver,
+			minor_ver);
+		return;
+	}
 
 	dev_dbg(asp->dev, "ASP endpoint is %d", asp->ep);
 
